.TH NBSP 1 "July 20, 2026" "nbsp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nbsp \- a small asynchronous prompt for macOS and Zsh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nbsp init zsh
.br
.B nbsp prompt
[
.B --status
.I N
]
[
.B --duration-ms
.I N
]
[
.B --jobs
.I N
]
.br
.B nbsp refresh
[
.B --cwd
.I PATH
]
[
.B --notify
]
.br
.B nbsp cache clear
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nbsp
renders an opinionated one-line Zsh prompt containing a shortened working
directory, Git status, active NVM version, command duration, background job
count, and the exact nonzero exit status. Failures render as a compact red
status joined to the prompt character, such as e1% or e127%.
.PP
The foreground renderer never executes Git. It reads the branch directly from
the repository metadata and consumes a small cached status snapshot. A
background refresh obtains porcelain-v2 status and asks ZLE to redraw the
prompt when ready.
.SH SETUP
Add the following after NVM initialization in
.IR ~/.zshrc :
.PP
.EX
eval "$(nbsp init zsh)"
.EE
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init zsh
Print the Zsh integration code.
.TP
.B prompt
Render a prompt using supplied command metadata and the current directory.
.TP
.B refresh
Refresh the Git snapshot for a directory. This is normally asynchronous.
.TP
.B cache clear
Remove cache and lock files owned by nbsp.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Set variables before running
.B init zsh.
The integration exports them for the native renderer.
.TP
.B NBSP_COLOR_PATH, NBSP_COLOR_GIT, NBSP_COLOR_NODE, NBSP_COLOR_META
Segment colors. Defaults: terminal foreground (default), terminal foreground
(default), green, and yellow.
.TP
.B NBSP_COLOR_OK, NBSP_COLOR_ERROR
Prompt character colors. Defaults: none and red.
.TP
.B NBSP_PROMPT_CHAR
Prompt character. Default: Zsh native %# (% normally, # when privileged).
Set it to $ to force a dollar prompt.
.TP
.B NBSP_DURATION_THRESHOLD_MS
Minimum duration to display. Default: 2000.
.TP
.B NBSP_GIT_TIMEOUT_MS
Background Git timeout. Default: 1500.
.TP
.B NBSP_SHOW_GIT, NBSP_SHOW_NVM, NBSP_SHOW_JOBS
Set any of these to 0 to hide the segment.
.TP
.B NBSP_CACHE_DIR
Override the cache root. The default is the XDG cache directory when set,
otherwise ~/Library/Caches/nbsp.
.SH GIT MARKERS
.B +
staged,
.B ~
modified,
.B ?
untracked,
.B !
conflicted,
.B ^
ahead,
.B v
behind, and
.B *
stashes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 2 for invalid command-line usage, and 1 for operational
refresh or cache failures. Optional prompt context failures do not prevent a
prompt from being rendered.
